  <title>Double entry transaction</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Double entry transaction</gui></guiseq>
  posts a transaction that no other window covers, such as moving money
  between two bank accounts, an owner's investment, or a correction your
  accountant gives you.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Type a <gui>Description</gui> and choose the
    <gui>Date</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Debit</gui>, click <gui>Add row</gui>, type the
    <gui>Amount</gui> and choose the <gui>Account</gui>. Add as many rows as
    the transaction needs.</p></item>
    <item><p>Do the same under <gui>Credit</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>When the two <gui>Total</gui>s match, click <gui>Post
    transaction</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Until the transaction can be posted, the button says what is wrong, for
  instance <gui>Credit and debit do not match</gui> or <gui>Debit account not
  selected</gui>. <gui>Delete row</gui> removes the selected row.
  <gui>Refresh accounts</gui> reloads the account lists after accounts are
  added in <link xref="accounts_configuration"/>.</p>

</page>
